  "summary": "An evidence-based approach to interior design that connects building occupants more closely with nature through integrated natural elements.",
  "description": "Incorporates direct nature views, natural materials, plants, water features, and biomorphic patterns to reduce stress and improve wellbeing. Growing from the biophilia hypothesis by E.O. Wilson, it's increasingly adopted in commercial and residential spaces for its health benefits and environmental connection.",
